# PublicIdpController — com.asrevo.cvhome.uaa.web.pub
#
# What the sign-in page asks before anyone is signed in. On uaa's own origin, anonymous, stateless.
# A hidden provider is not in the list but still answers discovery: hiding is about the button.

### the buttons — 200 PublicIdpDto[] {alias, displayName, preset, type, authorizationUrl}
GET {{UAA_URL}}/api/v1/public/idps

### home-realm discovery — 200 {"provider": PublicIdpDto | null}; never says whether an account exists
POST {{UAA_URL}}/api/v1/public/idps/discover
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "someone@example.com"}

### why the sign-in page is shown — 200 LoginContext {clientId, clientName, pendingLink}
# Reads the session's saved authorization request and any brokered login waiting for its password.
GET {{UAA_URL}}/api/v1/public/login/context

### start a brokered login — 302 to the provider's authorization endpoint (open in a browser)
# GET {{UAA_URL}}/oauth2/authorization/google?login_hint=someone@example.com
